From 48c10aa34585dc5b1e7fed7c9af7501286c114ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RafaelSMJF <43671981+RafaelSMJF@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 3 May 2026 11:29:59 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add xsim 2025.1 workarounds: ifndef XSIM guards

xsim 2025.1 has two categories of bugs requiring workarounds:

1. Kernel crash with non-power-of-2 packed struct arrays in always_comb
   store_buffer.sv: store_if body replaced with minimal loop-copy stub.
   The 131-bit struct (56+64+8+2+1) x4 elements causes FATAL_ERROR with
   any procedural logic beyond simple field-by-field copy.

2. $fatal assertions firing on X values during initialization
   Guards added to 13 files: wt_l15_adapter, wt_dcache_mem, wt_dcache_ctrl,
   wt_dcache_missunit, wt_dcache, scoreboard, load_unit, issue_read_operands,
   instr_queue, frontend, axi_shim, cache_ctrl, tag_cmp, std_nbdcache.

Pattern used: `ifndef XSIM inside existing `ifndef VERILATOR blocks.
These changes do not affect synthesis or non-xsim simulation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
