From 3c45c258ed22edb3c97738f094a6f9efb0773bf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RafaelSMJF <43671981+RafaelSMJF@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 3 May 2026 11:32:13 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add xsim 2025.1 workarounds: icache, assign->always_comb,
 wbuffer

Additional xsim 2025.1 bug workarounds:

- cva6_icache.sv: replace variable-index packed array accesses
  (cl_sel[hit_idx] and cl_offset_q-indexed accesses) that cause
  FATAL_ERROR when hit_idx=X; use one-hot mux and comparison loops instead
- csr_regfile.sv, decoder.sv: change assign to always_comb for
  packed-type casts (riscv::csr_t' and riscv::instruction_t') that
  crash xsim during elaboration
- wt_cache_subsystem.sv, wt_dcache_wbuffer.sv: add ifndef XSIM guards
  around $warning assertions
- ariane_verilog_wrap.sv: reduce wake_up_cnt width to 5 bits under XSIM
  to avoid xsim counter overflow crash

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 core/cache_subsystem/cva6_icache.sv        | 247 ++++++++++++---------
 core/cache_subsystem/wt_cache_subsystem.sv |   2 +
 core/cache_subsystem/wt_dcache_wbuffer.sv  |   4 +-
 core/csr_regfile.sv                        |   2 +-
 core/decoder.sv                            |   2 +-
 core/mmu_sv39/ptw.sv                       |   2 +-
 corev_apu/openpiton/ariane_verilog_wrap.sv |   4 +
 7 files changed, 155 insertions(+), 108 deletions(-)

